    "start": 229.609,
    "end": 237.874,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think there must be some reason for those students to say it's a custom made for West.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_33",
    "start": 237.954,
    "end": 238.174,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Yes.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_34",
    "start": 238.474,
    "end": 238.714,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Yes.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_35",
    "start": 240.633,
    "end": 251.219,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "So yes, to elaborate a little bit on that also, if we go into Vajrayana and skillful means, maybe how would you translate that?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_36",
    "start": 252.76,
    "end": 257.002,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "It's always hard to translate Tibetan terms into English terms and what they mean.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_37",
    "start": 258.383,
    "end": 262.546,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "And what do you think it means for Westerners, or for you maybe?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_38",
    "start": 269.123,
    "end": 279.106,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Generally, what I think, generally in Buddhism, it's really like I said the other day, it doesn't have an expiry date.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_39",
    "start": 280.386,
    "end": 289.229,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "It is made for sentient beings as long as we have suffering due to our negative emotions.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_40",
    "start": 289.849,
    "end": 291.63,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So it is to deal with negative emotions.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_41",
    "start": 292.69,
    "end": 311.148,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So, as we have so many different mindsets, each one has almost different kinds of mindsets, so therefore there are so many varieties of teachings from Hinayana, Mahayana, Vajrayana, depends on up to their different faculties.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_42",
    "start": 313.408,
    "end": 340.334,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think the Buddhism is always kind of relevant to whatever century we live in, or whatever we call these days, Gen Z, or Gen Millennium, or Gen Alpha, Gen Beta, even future Gen Betas will also benefit from this teaching.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_43",
    "start": 341.674,
    "end": 359.849,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "The most important thing is that the main teaching, the main kind of the message should not be lost in kind of modernizing or so-called modernizing or new age, all this kind of thing.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_44",
    "start": 360.509,
    "end": 374.061,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Of course we can, these things can be like a door, but when it really comes to the practice then I think, I don't know, that's my view, it's like, I think it's important to keep it to the real tradition.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_45",
    "start": 376.69,
    "end": 389.1,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "So maybe to bounce on that, would you have some hard advice to give maybe on aspiring Vajrayana practitioners or people who knew on the past or even older people on the past?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_46",
    "start": 389.58,
    "end": 391.702,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "How do they keep it authentic?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_47",
    "start": 391.742,
    "end": 395.004,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Interviewer",
    "text": "How do any message you'd like to maybe share?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_48",
    "start": 401.533,
    "end": 417.94,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I think, like I say, it has to be a little bit better when teachers or students, both sides, have to see exactly what teaching is that really fits your kind of mindset.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_49",
    "start": 417.98,
    "end": 426.044,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Sometimes, even someone who cannot really accept Vajrayana, suddenly jump into Vajrayana, then they could have wrong views and misunderstandings.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_50",
    "start": 426.985,
    "end": 433.29,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And then some people are ready to practice a very open mind and ready to practice Vajrayana, but it doesn't get the opportunity.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_51",
    "start": 434.21,
    "end": 439.835,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think very importantly is that to see that, like I mentioned, the Buddhism is very vast.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_52",
    "start": 439.975,
    "end": 441.977,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "There are so many different methods, so many teachings.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_53",
    "start": 442.657,
    "end": 446.06,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So we have to try to see which one really fits your mindset.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
